format: 2
name: a hexadecimal int literal with its top bit set has Java's value (T25, fixed)
class: Probe
method: m
expect: AGREE
note: JLS 21 §3.10.1: 0xFFFFFFFF as an int literal is -1, and 0x80000000 is -2147483648. JuLC read
note: them as unsigned. Fixed for T25: IntegerLiterals follows §3.10.1. Before the fix the expectation
note: was DIVERGE T25 Value/Value, the JVM returning -2147483648 and UPLC 6442450944.
---
import java.math.BigInteger;

public class Probe {
    public static BigInteger m() {
        int all = 0xFFFFFFFF;
        int top = 0x80000000;
        return BigInteger.valueOf(all).add(BigInteger.valueOf(top)).add(BigInteger.ONE);
    }
}
